WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.918
ClawDOS an AI

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.779
coding agent

00:00:03.318 --> 00:00:04.497
ClawDOS is an

00:00:04.368 --> 00:00:05.452
AI chat and

00:00:05.264 --> 00:00:06.395
coding harness for

00:00:06.207 --> 00:00:07.174
DOS running on

00:00:06.985 --> 00:00:08.200
an IBM PC

00:00:08.011 --> 00:00:09.178
5160

00:00:09.273 --> 00:00:10.570
with an 8088

00:00:10.441 --> 00:00:12.575
at 4.77 MHz

00:00:12.764 --> 00:00:14.744
640K of RAM

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:15.617
and CGA

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:16.749
using a bridge

00:00:16.561 --> 00:00:17.634
PC to handle

00:00:17.445 --> 00:00:18.294
TLS

00:00:18.814 --> 00:00:19.745
The author built

00:00:19.557 --> 00:00:20.347
it for fun

00:00:20.158 --> 00:00:21.125
on the restored

00:00:20.948 --> 00:00:22.151
IBM PC from

00:00:21.963 --> 00:00:22.847
his childhood

00:00:22.918 --> 00:00:23.979
which now boots

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.781
from an SD

00:00:24.592 --> 00:00:25.429
card through a

00:00:25.241 --> 00:00:26.325
PicoMEM

00:00:26.846 --> 00:00:27.742
Apart from the

00:00:27.554 --> 00:00:28.438
author's note

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.029
the whole repository

00:00:29.841 --> 00:00:30.654
was written by

00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:31.103
Claude

00:00:31.256 --> 00:00:32.376
as an experiment

00:00:32.188 --> 00:00:32.989
in how far

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:33.779
a coding agent

00:00:33.591 --> 00:00:34.345
can go under

00:00:34.157 --> 00:00:35.631
unusual constraints

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.164
Full story on

00:00:36.975 --> 00:00:37.871
the dashboard
